<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy temperature.</span>
The entropy temperature <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> controls how strongly LEAF-X favors
focused, low-entropy attention heads. Smaller values produce sharper
attributions but may over-concentrate on a few frames, while larger
values include more diffuse heads and reduce localization. As shown in
Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix E Component and Hyperparameter Ablations ‣ Listening with Attention: Entropy-Guided Explainability for Transformer-Based Audio Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> provides the best overall
trade-off between faithful speech explanations, acoustic evidence
localization, sparsity, and explanation robustness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A5.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity to entropy temperature <math id="A5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on
Whisper-large-v3 with LibriSpeech. Values follow the trend of the main component ablation and are intended as a compact hyperparameter study.</span></figcaption>
